    pr_ref:  # dc28
    description: "supply_chain_tier must name supply-chain DISTANCE only (ADR-0041 §1 axiom: \"no other fact may influence the value\"); it must NOT encode \"this is a synthetic node that must not be reclassified.\" Tier-axis concept audit (2026-07-15) found six linkers set supply_chain_tier=2 on SYNTHETIC nodes whose reason strings name a role/mechanism, never a distance: tauri_ipc.py:660/785/885/915 (\"synthetic IPC bridge/caller node\", \"synthetic Tauri event emitter/listener\"), wasm_bindgen.py:283/419 (\"synthetic WASM bridge node\"), message_dispatch.py:289/322 (\"message dispatch sender/handler\"), annotation_convention.py:216/251/352 (\"@hg:publishes/subscribes/dispatches annotation\"), yjs_crdt.py:425/457 (\"synthetic Yjs CRDT publisher/subscriber\"), solidity_abi.py:224. The tauri_ipc.py:660 comment is explicit: \"Tier 2 prevents _classify_symbols from reclassifying based on the host file path\" — the value 2 is chosen for its side-effect (cli.py:8397 skips symbols where tier != 1), a MECHANISM leaking into the distance axis (mechanism-vs-category leakage test).\n\nSTRUCTURAL FIX: a separate is_synthetic / classification-locked flag (or a supply_chain_reason-based skip) so _classify_symbols skips synthetic linker nodes WITHOUT borrowing tier-2; the synthetic nodes then carry an honest distance tier. Cross-ref: WI-zadot (needs_human_review — synthetic linker nodes kind=function/language=python mislabel), WI-vuzaf (synthetic-node id NAME slot vs node.name). Evidence + verdict: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-supply_chain_tier_07152026.md (F3)."  # dc28
    fields:  # dc28
      statement: "supply_chain_tier must name supply-chain distance only per ADR-0041 §1; six linkers set tier-2 on synthetic nodes for the _classify_symbols tier!=1 reclassification-skip side-effect, not for distance."  # dc28
      root_cause: "cli._classify_symbols skips symbols where supply_chain_tier != 1, so linkers borrow tier-2 as a reclassification-lock instead of declaring a separate is_synthetic/classification-locked flag; the tier field is the only available lock, so the mechanism leaked into the distance axis."  # dc28
